  "notes": "Atlantic County Republicans elect county committee members at large by municipality, not by election district: the June 2, 2026 primary ballot had a 'REP County Committee-at-Large - Male <municipality> (Vote For N)' and a matching Female contest in each of the 23 municipalities (Galloway has two separate at-large contests, Vote For 10 and Vote For 9, listed as printed). Each entry here is one at-large unit, so seats per unit vary and seats_per_precinct is null. The 2025 primary had no county committee contests and the 2024 primary had Democratic ones only, so 2026 is the latest Republican election. Filled = a ballot candidate finishing within the top N with votes (the Clarity export reports no write-in totals, so ballot winners cannot be compared with write-ins). Unknown = a tie at the last winning place (1 seat, in Hammonton; the other contested races in Hammonton and Mullica were decided). Seats with a 'NO PETITION FILED' placeholder line on the ballot are empty_no_filer: no candidate filed, and write-in results are not published, so a write-in could have won. Municipality names are as printed (e.g. 'Egg Hrbr City'; the female contest prints 'Egg Hrbr Cty' and was merged with it)."
